# sajinthiniMart — C++ Full Stack Capstone

An educational online shopping website with product images, search, category filter, cart, checkout demo, order history, seller product management, reviews API, admin user/order views, C++20, Drogon and SQLite.

## Important review-day notes
- The required stack in the supplied brief is C++20 + Drogon + PostgreSQL/SQLite + CMake + HTML/CSS/JavaScript + GitHub.
- This source is a starter implementation intended to run locally once the required C++ dependencies are installed. I cannot verify compilation in your environment from this ZIP alone.
- Product photographs are loaded from Unsplash URLs, so internet access is needed to display them.
- Demo admin login: `admin@yashimart.local` / `admin123`.
- Checkout is a simulation; no real payment is taken.
- For classroom use only: the sample login stores passwords as plain text and is NOT suitable for real users or deployment. Use hashed passwords and parameterized SQL before any public deployment.

## Requirements
- C++20 compiler
- CMake 3.20+
- Drogon C++ web framework
- SQLite3 development library

## Run in VS Code (Linux / Ubuntu lab)
Open this folder in VS Code. Open Terminal > New Terminal and run:

```bash
cmake -S . -B build
cmake --build build -j2
./build/yashimart
```

Then open `http://localhost:8080` in the browser. The SQLite database is created automatically at `data/yashimart.db`.

If CMake says Drogon or SQLite is missing, the lab computer needs those dependencies installed first. On Ubuntu, SQLite development files can be installed with `sudo apt install build-essential cmake libsqlite3-dev`; Drogon installation depends on the lab setup. Do not run installation commands on a managed lab computer without permission.

## Main API routes
- `GET /api/health` — backend/database status
- `GET /api/products?q=&category=` — search/filter products
- `POST /api/register` — buyer/seller registration
- `POST /api/login` — buyer/seller/admin login
- `POST /api/products` — add product
- `DELETE /api/products/{id}` — delete product
- `POST /api/orders` — place demo order
- `GET /api/orders?email=` — order history
- `GET /api/reviews?product_id=` / `POST /api/reviews` — product reviews
- `GET /api/admin/users` — list users
- `GET /api/admin/orders` — list orders

